<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
Hand-authored per TrackMate's documented XML model-export schema (Model > AllSpots >
SpotsInFrame > Spot, Model > AllTracks > Track > Edge) — NOT exported from a real Fiji/TrackMate
run (none is available in this environment; see src/benchmark.py's module docstring). This
fixture exists to verify load_trackmate_xml()'s parsing logic against the schema it claims to
implement. It is not a substitute for validating against a real exported file — do that before
trusting a comparison table that includes a real TrackMate row (see RUNBOOK.md step 8).

Encodes the same two-cell, one-division scenario as tests/test_benchmark.py's
_synthetic_dataset(), so a real comparison run and this fixture can be reasoned about side by
side: track 0 divides between frame 1 and frame 2 (spot 2 -> spots 4 and 5); track 1 runs
undivided for all four frames.
-->
